/target

# Drop-in vendor ESI catalogs are large (multi-MB) and not committed. Ignore
# every ESI file under esi/ ...
esi/*.xml
# ... but keep the trimmed single-device fixtures so the demo builds
# standalone from a clean checkout. A user can drop the full Beckhoff catalog
# files (e.g. `Beckhoff EL7xxx.xml`) into `esi/` to generate the whole device
# set; those large files stay local-only.
!esi/beckhoff_el1008.xml
!esi/beckhoff_el2004.xml
!esi/beckhoff_el7047.xml

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT tracked for this example: it depends on the
# unreleased in-tree taktora-connector-ethercat 0.3.1 (startup_sdos / REQ_0853)
# via the local-deps patch. A committed lock can only pin the published 0.3.0,
# which makes a patch-on build silently resolve the wrong version (the path
# patch is dropped as unused). Regenerate fresh: `scripts/examples-local.sh on`
# then build. Track it once connector-ethercat 0.3.1 is published to crates.io.
/Cargo.lock
